{
  "_comment": "Copy to .mcp.json and replace the paths below with absolute paths for your machine. Then restart Claude Code from this directory.",
  "_setup": [
    "1. git clone https://github.com/mixelpixx/KiCAD-MCP-Server somewhere (e.g. ~/programming/_tools/kicad-mcp).",
    "2. cd into it: npm install && npm run build",
    "3. brew install --cask kicad (KiCad 9 or 10).",
    "4. Install the server's Python deps into a side directory using KiCad's bundled Python (so they live with the tool, not inside the KiCad app bundle):",
    "     /Applications/KiCad/KiCad.app/Contents/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/Current/bin/pip3 install --target ~/programming/_tools/kicad-mcp/.venv-site -r ~/programming/_tools/kicad-mcp/requirements.txt",
    "   Then prepend that path to PYTHONPATH in the env block below (colon-separated, before the KiCad site-packages path).",
    "5. Replace the paths below with your machine's actual paths.",
    "6. cp .mcp.json.example .mcp.json",
    "7. Restart Claude Code; approve the project-scoped MCP server when prompted."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "kicad": {
      "command": "/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/node",
      "args": ["/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/kicad-mcp/dist/index.js"],
      "env": {
        "KICAD_PYTHON": "/Applications/KiCad/KiCad.app/Contents/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/Current/bin/python3",
        "PYTHONPATH": "/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/kicad-mcp/.venv-site:/Applications/KiCad/KiCad.app/Contents/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.9/lib/python3.9/site-packages",
        "LOG_LEVEL": "info"
      }
    }
  }
}
